 the second qualifier, White posted the highest score to make the final. In the final, White dominated the first run, with no judge’s score below 9.0. His 46.8 took a huge lead, and held up thru the second round to earn him the gold medal. Kass repeated his silver medal from Salt Lake City. Kass had struggled in the first run, but posted the best score in the second run to move up to second place. White was born with a congenital heart malformation, termed Tetralogy of Fallot (blue-baby syndrome), which required two surgeries to correct before he was a year old."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying Round 1"] [:th {} "Qualifying Round 2"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/109860"} "Shaun White"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "37.7 (7)"] [:td {} "45.3 (1)"] [:td {} "46.8 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/101112"} "Danny Kass"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "43.8 (1)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "44.0 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/101118"} "Markku Koski"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FIN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FIN.png"}] "FIN"]] [:td {} "20.2 (28)"] [:td {} "40.6 (3)"] [:td {} "41